  ('1028', 'Clinical Procedures and Instrumentation in Emergency Services', 3, $ahs${"academic_year": 3, "subjects": [{"subject_no": "Paper III", "title": "Clinical Procedures and Instrumentation in Emergency Services", "mode": "flat", "topics": ["INSTRUMENTATION IN EMERGENCY SERVICES: Introduction to Biomedical engineering (Man - machine relationship); ECG; DC Defibrillator; Intravenous pumps; Laryngoscope, ambubag, suction machine; SPO2 monitoring, Temperaure monitoring; BP apparatus, BP monitoring - NIBP, IBP; Ventilators - Intensive care, portable; Power generation, transmission & distribution; Manual resuscitator; Radiology equipment & radiation hazards; Suction machine; Nebuliser; Medical gases; Ambulance and its power supply; Dialysis machine; Infant warmer & incubator", "CLINICAL PROCEDURES IN EMERGENCY ROOM - Vital Sign Measurement: Pulse assessment; Respiratory assessment; Temperature assessment; Blood pressure assessment", "CLINICAL PROCEDURES IN EMERGENCY ROOM - Respiratory procedures: Endotracheal intubation and extubation; Drugs through ET tube; Tracheostomy insertion and management; Suctioning an artificial airway; Naso tracheal suctioning; Insertion of nasopharyngeal and oropharyngeal airway; Mechanical ventilation; Intercostal drain; age; Thoracocentesis", "CLINICAL PROCEDURES IN EMERGENCY ROOM - Intermediate Airways: Laryngeal Mask Airway; Esophageal - Tracheal Combitube", "CLINICAL PROCEDURES IN EMERGENCY ROOM - Non invasive Assessment and Support of Oxygenation and Ventilation: Pulse oximetry; Carbon dioxide Monitoring --> Capnometry; Oxygen therapy; Delivery systems for Inhaled Medication - Nebulizers, Metered Dose Inhaler", "CLINICAL PROCEDURES IN EMERGENCY ROOM - Cardiovascular procedures: Cardiac Monitoring; Central venous pressure monitoring; Insertion of Arterial line; Central venous cannulation; Transcutaneous cardiac pacing; Transvenous cardiac pacing; Pericardiocentesis; Cardioversion; Defibrillation", "CLINICAL PROCEDURES IN EMERGENCY ROOM - Cannulating Umbilical Vein: Indication; Procedure; Drugs through umbilical vein; Complication", "CLINICAL PROCEDURES IN EMERGENCY ROOM - Intraosseous Infusion: Indication; Procedure; Drugs through intraosseous line; Complication", "CLINICAL PROCEDURES IN EMERGENCY ROOM - Gastrointestinal procedures: Insertion of nasogastric tube; Insertion of enteral feeding tube and initiation of feedings; Gastric lavage; Upper gastrointestinal endoscopy; Insertion of rectal tube; Paracentesis; Peritoneal lavage", "CLINICAL PROCEDURES IN EMERGENCY ROOM - Poison decontamination: Activated charcoal; Whole bowl irrigation", "CLINICAL PROCEDURES IN EMERGENCY ROOM - Genitourinary procedures: Urethral catheterization; Peritoneal dialysis; Placement and Management of external Arteriovenous shunt; Continuous Arteriovenous hemofiltration", "CLINICAL PROCEDURES IN EMERGENCY ROOM - Intravenous Therapy: Insertion of intravenous catheter; Administration of parenteral nutrition; Blood administration", "CLINICAL PROCEDURES IN EMERGENCY ROOM - Neurologic Procedures: Lumbar Puncture"], "units": [], "reference_books": [], "notes": "Titled 'Clinical Procedures and Instruments Emergency Services' in source, shown as PAPER-3 in III YEAR. Practicals: ECG - Power supply testing, Fuses testing, Spot identification (Thermometer, BP apparatus, Stethoscope, Glucometer, Intraosseous infusion, LMA, Combitube, ET intubation, Nebuliser, Ventilator, Capnography, Pulse oximeter). No dedicated reference book in the combined reference list maps specifically to this paper."}], "intro": "Titled 'Clinical Procedures and Instruments Emergency Services' in source, shown as PAPER-3 in III YEAR. Practicals: ECG - Power supply testing, Fuses testing, Spot identification (Thermometer, BP apparatus, Stethoscope, Glucometer, Intraosseous infusion, LMA, Combitube, ET intubation, Nebuliser, Ventilator, Capnography, Pulse oximeter). No dedicated reference book in the combined reference list maps specifically to this paper."}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"components": [{"name": "Internal Assessment", "max": 50, "min": 25}, {"name": "Theory (University)", "max": 100, "min": 50}, {"name": "Practical", "max": 50, "min": 25}, {"name": "Viva voce", "max": 50, "min": 25}], "question_pattern": {"duration_hours": null, "sections": [], "total_marks": 100}, "notes": "Scheme of Examination is per year/paper (not uniform across all papers). FIRST YEAR - Paper 1 (Anatomy, Physiology, Biochemistry) and Paper 2 (Introduction to Emergency Medicine (EM) and EMS-I): Internal assessment 50/25, Theory 100/50, Practical 50/25, Total 200/100 each. Paper 3 (Computer Science) and Paper 4 (English) are Internal Examination only (Note: 'Paper 3 and Paper 4 is Internal Examination'). SECOND YEAR - Paper 1 (Pathology, Microbiology, Pharmacology): Internal assessment 50/25, Theory 100/50, Total 150/75. Paper 2 (Patient examination and Nursing): Internal assessment 50/25, Theory 100/50, Total 150/75. Paper 3 (Emergency Medicine (EM) and EMS-II / Practical exam on Patient Examination, Nursing, Triage, Life Support, Trauma care): Internal assessment 50/25, Theory 100/50, Practical 50/25, Viva voce 50/25, Total 250/125. THIRD YEAR - Paper 1 (Emergency Medicine (EM) and EMS-III): Internal assessment 50/25, Theory 100/50, Practical 50/25, Total 200/100. Paper 2 (Emergency surgery & Emergency Surgical Services): Internal assessment 50/25, Theory 100/50, Total 150/75. Paper 3 (Clinical Procedures and Instrumentation in Emergency Services): Internal assessment 50/25, Theory 100/50, Practical 50/25, Total 200/100. Source specifies no theory question paper duration or section pattern. Internal assessment for English = Term test 30 marks + Assignment 20 marks (English total 100 marks). Computers (Introduction to Computers) Weightage of marks 25: Term test 15 marks + Assignment 10 marks. Internal Assessment 50 marks stated as Term tests 30 + assignments 20 for Microbiology.", "source_academic_year": "2014-15"}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"total_duration": "", "postings": [], "notes": "No internship section is provided in the source document for this program."}$ahs$::jsonb),
  ('1131', 'Basic sciences', 1, $ahs${"academic_year": 1, "subjects": [{"subject_no": "Paper I", "title": "Basic sciences", "mode": "flat", "topics": [{"title": "BASIC ANATOMY - THEORY", "content": "Introduction to Anatomy. Basic Anatomical terminologies. Osteology - Upper limb - clavicle, scapula, humerus, radius, ulna; Lower limb - femur, hipbone, sacrum, tibia, fibula; Vertebral column. Thorax - Intercostal space, pleura, bony thoracic cage, ribs, sternum & thoracic vertebrae, Muscles of Thorax, Diaphragm, Lungs. Airway - Larynx, Trachea, bronchial tree. Heart - Surface anatomy of heart, chambers of the heart, valves of the heart, major blood vessels of heart, pericardium, coronary arteries. Excretory system - Kidneys, ureters, bladder, urethra. Liver. Central Nervous system."}, {"title": "BASIC ANATOMY - PRACTICALS", "content": "Mannequins to be provided for Teaching. Osteology - Bones identification (right and left side) and prominent features of clavicle, scapula, radius, ulna, humerus, femur, hip bone, sacrum, tibia, fibula. Surface Anatomy. Radiology, X-ray Chest PA view, X-ray of limbs and X-ray abdomen: Names Views and identification. Specimens/Models, OSPE charts."}, {"title": "PHYSIOLOGY - THEORY", "content": "1) The Cell: (i) Cell Structure and functions of the various organelles. (ii) Endocytosis and exocytosis. (iii) Neuro muscular junction. 2) The Blood: (i) Composition of Blood, functions of the blood and plasma proteins; (ii) Function of Hemoglobin; (iii) Erythrocyte Sedimentation Rate; (iv) Detailed description about WBC - Total count (TC), Differential count (DC) and functions; (v) Platelets - formation and normal level and functions; (vi) Blood groups and Rh factor. 3) CardioVascular System: (i) Physiology of the heart; (ii) Heart sounds; (iii) Cardiac cycle, Cardiac output; (iv) Auscultatory areas; (v) Arterial pressures, blood pressure; (vi) Hypertension; (vii) Electro cardiogram (ECG); (viii) Cardio Pulmonary Resuscitation. 4) Respiratory system: (i) Respiratory movements; Oxygen saturation of Blood, Pulse Oximeter; Surfactants and Normal values of Lung volumes and Lung capacities; Diffusion. 5) Excretory system: (i) Normal Urinary output; (ii) Micturation; (iii) Renal function tests. 6) Reproductive system: (i) Reproductive organs; (ii) Brief account of menstrual cycle. 7) Central Nervous system: (i) Functions of CSF; (ii) Functions of Cortex; (iii) Sleep cycle; (iv) Reticular activating system. 8) Endocrine system: Functions of the pituitary, thyroid, parathyroid, adrenal and pancreatic Hormones. 9) Digestive system: (i) Physiological Anatomy of the GIT; (ii) Food Digestion in the mouth, stomach, intestine; (iii) Absorption of foods and gastric emptying; (iv) Role of bile in the digestion; (v) Vomiting mechanism."}, {"title": "PHYSIOLOGY - PRACTICAL", "content": "1) The Compound Microscope. 2) Determination of Pulse rate - Details on Pulse. 3) Determination of Blood Groups. 4) Measurement of human blood pressure. 5) Examination of Respiratory system to count respiratory rate and measure inspiration and Expiration."}, {"title": "BIOCHEMISTRY - Cellular Metabolism", "content": "(I) Enzymes. (II) Coenzymes. (III) Glucose Metabolism. (IV) Urea Cycles. (V) Protein & lipid - Classifications and functions. Vitamins & Minerals: Fat soluble vitamins (A, D, E, K) - Water soluble vitamins - B complex vitamins - principal elements (Calcium, Phosphorus, Magnesium, Sodium, Potassium, Chlorine and sulphur) - Trace elements - Basal metabolic rate (BMR) - respiratory quotient (RQ) - Specific dynamic action (SDA) - Balanced diet - Nutritional deficiency like Marasmus - and Kwashiorkar. Acids and bases: Definition, pH, Henderson - Hasselbalch equation, Buffers, Indicators, Normality, Molarity, Molality, Blood Gas Analysis."}, {"title": "BIOCHEMISTRY - SYLLABUS FOR PRACTICALS", "content": "1. Benedict's test. 2. Heat coagulation tests."}, {"title": "PATHOLOGY", "content": "1. Cellular adaptation, Cell injury & cell death. Introduction to pathology. Overview: Cellular response to stress and noxious stimuli. Cellular adaptations of growth and differentiation. Overview of cell injury and cell death. Causes of cell injury. Mechanisms of cell injury. Reversible and irreversible cell injury. Examples of cell injury and necrosis. 2. Inflammation. General features of inflammation. Acute inflammation. Chemical mediators of inflammation. Chronic inflammation. 3. Immunity disorders. General features of the immune system. Disorders of the immune system. Hyper sensitivity reaction - I, II, III, IV. 4. Infectious diseases. General principles of microbial pathogenesis. Viral infections - HBV, HCV, HIV, CMV. Bacterial infections - streptococci, E. Coli, Salmonella, Staphylococci, Tuberculosis. Fungal infections. Parasitic infections. TORCH infection. 5. Neoplasia. Definition. Nomenclature. Biology of tumor growth benign and malignant neoplasms. Carcinogenic agents and their cellular interactions. Clinical features of tumors. 6. Environmental and nutritional disorders. Occupational Hazards. Radiation injury. Marasmus. Kwashiorkar."}, {"title": "PATHOLOGY - PRACTICAL SYLLABUS", "content": "Specimens, Models, OSPE, Stations, CHARTS."}, {"title": "CLINICALS/THEATRES (I Year, 12 hours per week in the mornings)", "content": "1. IV fluids and Transfusion related matters. 2. Dressing, sutures, bandages and plasters. 3. Recovery room and nursing care. 4. Pre-Operative and Post-Operative Management of Patients. 5. Patient handling and Transportation to and from the Operation theatre. 6. Universal precautions for HIV Positives, HBsAg Positive. 7. Introduction to Operating room - Ethics, Discipline, Lay out, Equipments - Lights, OT table, suction, scrub station. 8. Electrical Devices - Electro cautery, Laser, Harmonic, Ligasure. 9. Power Surgical Instruments - Drills, Saw, Reamer. 10. Common General Surgical Operations and Dressings."}], "units": [], "reference_books": [], "notes": "Year I 'Basic Science' paper. Basic Sciences mark allocation: Anatomy 30%, Physiology 30%, Biochemistry 20%, Pathology 20%. ENGLISH and BASICS OF COMPUTER SCIENCE are taught in Year I but form the separate 'Basics of Computer Science and English' internal paper (not part of this Basic Sciences paper / not in the OTAT paper list). No reference books listed in source."}], "intro": "Year I 'Basic Science' paper. Basic Sciences mark allocation: Anatomy 30%, Physiology 30%, Biochemistry 20%, Pathology 20%. ENGLISH and BASICS OF COMPUTER SCIENCE are taught in Year I but form the separate 'Basics of Computer Science and English' internal paper (not part of this Basic Sciences paper / not in the OTAT paper list). No reference books listed in source."}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"components": [{"name": "Theory (University)", "max": 100, "min": 50}, {"name": "Practical", "max": 100, "min": 50}, {"name": "Viva", "max": 50, "min": 25}, {"name": "Internal Assessment", "max": 50, "min": 25}], "question_pattern": {"duration_hours": null, "sections": [], "total_marks": 100}, "notes": "Exam pattern per Examination Pattern I/II/III Year tables: Theory MAX 100 / MIN 50; Practical MAX 100 / MIN 50; Viva MAX 50 / MIN 25; Internal Assessment MAX 50 (MIN shown as 20 for the first subject each year and 25 for the others). Year I: (1) BASIC SCIENCES; (2) BASICS OF COMPUTER SCIENCE AND ENGLISH. Marks in Basic Sciences to be allotted as Anatomy 30% - Physiology 30% - Biochemistry 20% & Pathology 20%. Basics of Computer Science and English will be an internal paper - Institution will send the marks to the University. Source does not specify examination duration or theory question-paper section breakdown."}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"total_duration": "One year", "postings": [], "notes": "Section header: \"POSTINGS DURING ONE YEAR INTERNSHIP\". The posting rotation lines in the source are corrupted/interleaved by OCR and cannot be reconstructed verbatim with confidence. Raw source fragments: \"Post Operative room / Recovery room - 3 months\", \"Sterilisation room ... 3 months\", \"Medical / Surgical Posting room (Including Post record room)\", \"Operation Theatre 3 months including Surgical ICU\", \"Casualty & OT\", \"General surgery OT\", \"Obstetrics & Gynaecology OT\", \"Paediatrics\", durations \"15 days / 1 month\". Postings left empty to avoid fabrication."}$ahs$::jsonb),
  ('1136', 'pharmacology and microbiology', 2, $ahs${"academic_year": 2, "subjects": [{"subject_no": "Paper I", "title": "pharmacology and microbiology", "mode": "flat", "topics": [{"title": "Pharmacology", "content": "ANTISIALAGOGUES - Atropine, Glycopyrrolate. SEDATIVES / ANXIOLYTICS - Diazepam, Midazolam, Phenergan, Lorazepam, Chloropromazine, Trichlophos. NARCOTICS - Morphine, Pethidine, Fentanyl, Pentazocine. ANTIEMETICS - Metoclopramide, Ondansetron, Dexamethasone. ANTACIDS - Na citrate, Gelusil, Mucaine gel. H2 BLOCKERS - Cimetidine, Ranitidine, Famotidine. INDUCTION AGENT - Thiopentone, Diazepam, Midazolam, Ketamine, Propofol, Etomidate. MUSCLE RELAXANTS - Depolarising: Suxamethonium; Non depolarising: Pancuronium, Vecuronium, Atracurium, Rocuronium. INTRODUCTION TO GENERAL ANAESTHESIA. INHALATIONAL GASES - Gases: O2, N2O, Air; Agents: Ether, Halothane, Isoflurane, Sevoflurane, Desflurane. REVERSAL AGENTS - Neostigmine, Glycopyrrolate, Atropine, Nalorphine, Naloxone, Flumazenil (Diazepam). ANTISEPTICS AND DISINFECTANTS. STERILISATION AND CLEANING OF SURGICAL EQUIPMENTS. LOCAL ANAESTHETICS - Xylocaine, Preparation, Local - Bupivacaine - Topical, Prilocaine jelly, Emla - Ointment, Etidocaine, Ropivacaine. EMERGENCY DRUGS - Adrenaline: Mode of administration, dilution, dosage, Effects, Isoprenaline; Atropine, bicarbonate, calcium, ephedrine, xylocard; Ionotropes: dopamine, dobutamine, amidarone; Aminophylline, hydrocortisone, antihistaminics, potassium; Cardiovascular drugs; Antihypertensives; Antiarrhythmics; Beta - Blockers; Ca - Channel blockers; Vasodilators - nitroglycerin & sodium nitroprusside; Respiratory system - Bronchodilators, respiratory stimulants, Broncholytic agents; Renal system - Diuretics, furosemide, mannitol; Obstetrics - oxytocin, methergin; Miscellaneous - Antibiotics, NSAIDS, Anticoagulants and Insulin."}, {"title": "Pharmacology - SYLLABUS FOR PRACTICALS", "content": "Specimens, drugs, OSPE charts."}, {"title": "Microbiology", "content": "Sterilization & decontamination - Dry; Filtration; General Principles Asepsis. Wound Infection & Urinary Tract Infections. Blood stream Infections. Respiratory tract Infection. S. Typhi, Salmonella Paratyphi 'A', Salmonella Typhimurium. Catheter, IV associated Infections. Hospital acquired infections & prevention of hospital acquired infections. Hepatitis C, HBV, HIV. Hyper sensitivity reaction - Type I, II, III, IV. Biomedical Waste Management."}, {"title": "Microbiology - SYLLABUS FOR PRACTICALS", "content": "Biomedical waste management, colour code. OSPE charts."}, {"title": "CLINICALS/THEATRES (II Year, 12 hours per week in the mornings)", "content": "1. Sterilization assembly and packing. 2. Principles of Sterile Techniques - Surgical scrub, gowning and gloving. 3. Surgical instrumentation, handling instruments."}], "units": [], "reference_books": [], "notes": "No reference books listed in source."}], "intro": "No reference books listed in source."}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"components": [{"name": "Theory (University)", "max": 100, "min": 50}, {"name": "Practical", "max": 100, "min": 50}, {"name": "Viva", "max": 50, "min": 25}, {"name": "Internal Assessment", "max": 50, "min": 25}], "question_pattern": {"duration_hours": null, "sections": [], "total_marks": 100}, "notes": "Exam pattern per Examination Pattern I/II/III Year tables: Theory MAX 100 / MIN 50; Practical MAX 100 / MIN 50; Viva MAX 50 / MIN 25; Internal Assessment MAX 50 (MIN shown as 20 for the first subject each year and 25 for the others). Year I: (1) BASIC SCIENCES; (2) BASICS OF COMPUTER SCIENCE AND ENGLISH. Marks in Basic Sciences to be allotted as Anatomy 30% - Physiology 30% - Biochemistry 20% & Pathology 20%. Basics of Computer Science and English will be an internal paper - Institution will send the marks to the University. Source does not specify examination duration or theory question-paper section breakdown."}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"total_duration": "One year", "postings": [], "notes": "Section