  ('1137', 'Medicine and medical ethics', 2, $ahs${"academic_year": 2, "subjects": [{"subject_no": "Paper II", "title": "Medicine and medical ethics", "mode": "flat", "topics": [{"title": "MEDICINE", "content": "1. Disorder of haemopoiesis - Anaemias - iron deficiency anaemia. 2. Infectious diseases - Sepsis and septic shock, fever of unknown origin, infective endocarditis, infection of skin, muscle, soft tissue, infection control in hospital, diseases caused by bacteria, viruses, mycobacterium, fungi and protozoa and helminthes, common secondary infection in HIV. 3. Diseases of CVS - congenital RHD, Rheumatic fever, CAD, Peripheral vascular diseases. 4. Respiratory system - asthma, pneumonia. 5. Kidney & Urinary tract - acute renal failure, Glomerulonephritis, Haemodialysis, Transplant, Urinary tract infection. 6. Liver and biliary tract disease - Viral hepatitis, alcoholism. 7. Endocrinology and metabolism - Diabetes mellitus, Hyper- and hypothyroidism. 8. Pain Medicine."}, {"title": "MEDICAL ETHICS", "content": "1. Medical ethics - Definition - Goal - Scope - therapy. 2. Code of conduct - Introduction. 3. Basic principles of medical ethics - Confidentiality. 4. Malpractice and negligence - Rational and irrational drug. 5. Autonomy and informed consent - Right of patients. 6. Care of the terminally ill - Euthanasia. 8. Organ transplantation. 9. Medico legal aspects of medical records - Medicolegal case and type, Records and document related to MLC, ownership of medical records, Confidentiality, Privilege communication, Release of medical information, Unauthorized disclosure, retention of medical records, other various aspects."}, {"title": "SYLLABUS FOR PRACTICALS", "content": "Specimens. OSPE charts."}], "units": [], "reference_books": [], "notes": "Numbering in source Medical Ethics section skips 7 (goes 1-6, then 8, 9), preserved as in source. No reference books listed in source."}], "intro": "Numbering in source Medical Ethics section skips 7 (goes 1-6, then 8, 9), preserved as in source. No reference books listed in source."}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"components": [{"name": "Theory (University)", "max": 100, "min": 50}, {"name": "Practical", "max": 100, "min": 50}, {"name": "Viva", "max": 50, "min": 25}, {"name": "Internal Assessment", "max": 50, "min": 25}], "question_pattern": {"duration_hours": null, "sections": [], "total_marks": 100}, "notes": "Exam pattern per Examination Pattern I/II/III Year tables: Theory MAX 100 / MIN 50; Practical MAX 100 / MIN 50; Viva MAX 50 / MIN 25; Internal Assessment MAX 50 (MIN shown as 20 for the first subject each year and 25 for the others). Year I: (1) BASIC SCIENCES; (2) BASICS OF COMPUTER SCIENCE AND ENGLISH. Marks in Basic Sciences to be allotted as Anatomy 30% - Physiology 30% - Biochemistry 20% & Pathology 20%. Basics of Computer Science and English will be an internal paper - Institution will send the marks to the University. Source does not specify examination duration or theory question-paper section breakdown."}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"total_duration": "One year", "postings": [], "notes": "Section header: \"POSTINGS DURING ONE YEAR INTERNSHIP\". The posting rotation lines in the source are corrupted/interleaved by OCR and cannot be reconstructed verbatim with confidence. Raw source fragments: \"Post Operative room / Recovery room - 3 months\", \"Sterilisation room ... 3 months\", \"Medical / Surgical Posting room (Including Post record room)\", \"Operation Theatre 3 months including Surgical ICU\", \"Casualty & OT\", \"General surgery OT\", \"Obstetrics & Gynaecology OT\", \"Paediatrics\", durations \"15 days / 1 month\". Postings left empty to avoid fabrication."}$ahs$::jsonb),
  ('1138', 'principles of anesthesia -I', 2, $ahs${"academic_year": 2, "subjects": [{"subject_no": "Paper III", "title": "principles of anesthesia -I", "mode": "flat", "topics": [{"title": "1. MEDICAL GAS SUPPLY", "content": "Compressed gas cylinders. Colour coding. Cylinder valves; pin index. Gas piping system. Recommendations for piping system. Alarms & safety devices."}, {"title": "2. ANAESTHESIA MACHINE", "content": "Hanger and yoke system. Cylinder pressure gauge. Pressure regulator. Flow meter assembly. Vapourizers - types, hazards, maintenance, filling and draining, etc."}, {"title": "3. BREATHING SYSTEM", "content": "General considerations: humidity & heat. Common components - connectors, adaptors, reservoir bags. Capnography ETCO2. Pulse oximetry. Methods of humidification. Classification of breathing system - Mapleson system a b c d e f, Jackson Rees system, Bain circuit. Non rebreathing valves - ambu valves. The circle system Components - Soda lime, indicators."}, {"title": "4. FACE MASKS & AIRWAY LARYNGOSCOPES", "content": "Types, sizes. Endotracheal tubes - Types, sizes. Cuff system. Fixing, removing and inflating cuff, checking tube position, complications. Bougie. LMA."}, {"title": "5. ANAESTHESIA VENTILATOR AND WORKING PRINCIPLES", "content": "Anaesthesia ventilator and working principles."}, {"title": "6. MONITORING", "content": "ECG. SpO2. Temperature. IBP. CVP. PA Pressure. LA Pressure. Bio Medical engineering of Trouble sorting Management, care of cleaning."}, {"title": "7. BASIC ANAESTHETIC TECHNIQUES / INTRODUCTION TO ANAESTHESIA", "content": "General Anaesthesia. Regional Anaesthesia. Local Anaesthesia. Intravenous Anaesthesia. Minimum standard of anaesthesia. Who should give anaesthesia? PREOP PREPARATION: Pre anaesthetic assessment - History, past history - disease / Surgery / and personal history - Smoking / alcohol; General physical assessment, systemic examination - CVS, RS, CNS. INVESTIGATIONS - Haematological their significance; Routine - Urine; Chest X-ray; Echocardiography; Angiography; Liver function test; Renal function test; Others. Case acceptance: ASA grading - I, II, III, IV, V. PRE-ANAESTHETIC ORDERS: Patient - Informed consent, NPO guidelines, Premedication - advantages, drugs used, Special instructions - if any; Machine - Checking the machine, O2, N2O, suction apparatus, Laryngoscopes, ET tubes, airways, Things for IV accessibility, Other monitoring systems; Drugs - Emergency drugs, Anaesthetic drugs. INTRAOPERATIVE MANAGEMENT - Confirm the identification of the patient; Monitoring - minimum; Non-invasive & Invasive monitoring; Induction - drugs used; Endotracheal intubation; Maintenance of anaesthesia; Positioning of the patient; Blood / fluid & electrolyte balance; Reversal from anaesthesia - drugs used; Transferring the patient; Recovery room - set up and things needed. POST OPERATIVE COMPLICATIONS & MANAGEMENT - Recovery and Delayed recovery; Hypoxia and Oxygen Therapy; PONV. 8. Basic Life Support - Cardio Pulmonary Resuscitation."}, {"title": "SYLLABUS FOR PRACTICALS", "content": "Instruments. Gas cylinders."}], "units": [], "reference_books": [], "notes": "No reference books listed in source."}], "intro": "No reference books listed in source."}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"components": [{"name": "Theory (University)", "max": 100, "min": 50}, {"name": "Practical", "max": 100, "min": 50}, {"name": "Viva", "max": 50, "min": 25}, {"name": "Internal Assessment", "max": 50, "min": 25}], "question_pattern": {"duration_hours": null, "sections": [], "total_marks": 100}, "notes": "Exam pattern per Examination Pattern I/II/III Year tables: Theory MAX 100 / MIN 50; Practical MAX 100 / MIN 50; Viva MAX 50 / MIN 25; Internal Assessment MAX 50 (MIN shown as 20 for the first subject each year and 25 for the others). Year I: (1) BASIC SCIENCES; (2) BASICS OF COMPUTER SCIENCE AND ENGLISH. Marks in Basic Sciences to be allotted as Anatomy 30% - Physiology 30% - Biochemistry 20% & Pathology 20%. Basics of Computer Science and English will be an internal paper - Institution will send the marks to the University. Source does not specify examination duration or theory question-paper section breakdown."}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"total_duration": "One year", "postings": [], "notes": "Section header: \"POSTINGS DURING ONE YEAR INTERNSHIP\". The posting rotation lines in the source are corrupted/interleaved by OCR and cannot be reconstructed verbatim with confidence. Raw source fragments: \"Post Operative room / Recovery room - 3 months\", \"Sterilisation room ... 3 months\", \"Medical / Surgical Posting room (Including Post record room)\", \"Operation Theatre 3 months including Surgical ICU\", \"Casualty & OT\", \"General surgery OT\", \"Obstetrics & Gynaecology OT\", \"Paediatrics\", durations \"15 days / 1 month\". Postings left empty to avoid fabrication."}$ahs$::jsonb),
  ('1141', 'sterilization procedures', 3, $ahs${"academic_year": 3, "subjects": [{"subject_no": "Paper I", "title": "sterilization procedures", "mode": "flat", "topics": [{"title": "1. Waste disposal", "content": "Waste disposal - collection of used items from user area, reception, protective clothing and disinfections safe guards, Bio-Medical wastes, Colour coding and management."}, {"title": "2. Use of disinfections", "content": "Use of disinfections - sorting and classification of equipment for cleaning purposes, sharps, blunt, lighted etc., contaminated high risk baby care, delicate instruments or hot care instruments."}, {"title": "3. Cleaning process", "content": "Cleaning process - use of detergents. Mechanical cleaning apparatus, cleaning instruments. Cleaning jars, receivers, bowls etc., trays, basins and similar hand ware utensils. Cleaning of catheters and tubings, cleaning glass ware, cleaning syringes and needles."}, {"title": "4. Materials used for wrapping and packing", "content": "Materials used for wrapping and packing, assembling pack contents. Types of packs prepared. Inclusion of trays and galliparts in packs. Method of wrapping and making use of indications to show that a pack or container has been through a sterilization process - date stamping."}, {"title": "5. General observations - principles of sterilization", "content": "General observations - principles of sterilization. Moist heat. Dry heat sterilization. EO gas sterilization. H2O2 gas plasma capo sterilization."}, {"title": "SYLLABUS FOR PRACTICALS", "content": "OSPE charts, Instruments."}, {"title": "CLINICALS/THEATRES (III Year, 12 hours per week in the mornings)", "content": "1. Routine Maintenance of Equipments and Instruments. 2. Laying out of Instrument, trolleys. 3. Emphasis on Surgical Positions, Instruments required and the role of Theatre Assistant in various surgeries. 4. Preparation of patient, aseptic techniques and draping. 5. Special Instrument like Laproscope, Endoscope, Monitors, C-arm. 6. Trouble shooting in OT. 7. Specimen labelling and handling. 8. Exposure to Critical Care Unit for Surgical patients."}], "units": [], "reference_books": [], "notes": "OTAT Year-3 Paper I code corrected to 1141 per paper list. No reference books listed in source."}], "intro": "OTAT Year-3 Paper I code corrected to 1141 per paper list. No reference books listed in source."}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"components": [{"name": "Theory (University)", "max": 100, "min": 50}, {"name": "Practical", "max": 100, "min": 50}, {"name": "Viva", "max": 50, "min": 25}, {"name": "Internal Assessment", "max": 50, "min": 25}], "question_pattern": {"duration_hours": null, "sections": [], "total_marks": 100}, "notes": "Exam pattern per Examination Pattern I/II/III Year tables: Theory MAX 100 / MIN 50; Practical MAX 100 / MIN 50; Viva MAX 50 / MIN 25; Internal Assessment MAX 50 (MIN shown as 20 for the first subject each year and 25 for the others). Year I: (1) BASIC SCIENCES; (2) BASICS OF COMPUTER SCIENCE AND ENGLISH. Marks in Basic Sciences to be allotted as Anatomy 30% - Physiology 30% - Biochemistry 20% & Pathology 20%. Basics of Computer Science and English will be an internal paper - Institution will send the marks to the University. Source does not specify examination duration or theory question-paper section breakdown."}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"total_duration": "One year", "postings": [], "notes": "Section header: \"POSTINGS DURING ONE YEAR INTERNSHIP\". The posting rotation lines in the source are corrupted/interleaved by OCR and cannot be reconstructed verbatim with confidence. Raw source fragments: \"Post Operative room / Recovery room - 3 months\", \"Sterilisation room ... 3 months\", \"Medical / Surgical Posting room (Including Post record room)\", \"Operation Theatre 3 months including Surgical ICU\", \"Casualty & OT\", \"General surgery OT\", \"Obstetrics & Gynaecology OT\", \"Paediatrics\", durations \"15 days / 1 month\". Postings left empty to avoid fabrication."}$ahs$::jsonb),
  ('1142', 'principles of anesthesia -II', 3, $ahs${"academic_year": 3, "subjects": [{"subject_no": "Paper II", "title": "principles of anesthesia -II", "mode": "flat", "topics": [{"title": "Regional Anaesthetic techniques", "content": "a. Local anaesthetic technique. b. Nerve blocks. c. Spinal Anaesthesia. d. Epidural anaesthesia."}, {"title": "NEURO ANAESTHESIA", "content": "Glasgow coma scale. Premedication. Special investigation - CT, Angiography and MRI. Checklist. Induction of a patient. Reinforced Endotracheal tubes. Positioning in neuro surgery. I.C.P. Air embolism. Reversal of the patient. Transferring to I.C.U. / Ward."}, {"title": "OBSTETRIC ANAESTHESIA", "content": "Differences between a pregnant and a normal lady. Risks for anaesthesia. Precautions to be taken. Check list. Regional vs general anaesthesia. Induction / maintenance and recovery. Resuscitation of the new born, APGAR score. Reversal and extubation. Emergencies - manual removal of placenta, A.P.H., P.P.H., Ruptured uterus, Ectopic Pregnancy."}, {"title": "PAEDIATRIC ANAESTHESIA", "content": "Theatre setting. Check list. Fluid Calculation and administration. Premedication - modes. Induction. Intubation - Securing the ETT. Reversal & extubation - Problems. Transferring / ICU management. Pain management."}, {"title": "ENT Anaesthesia", "content": "Anaesthesia for adenotonsillectomy. Anaesthesia for mastoidectomy. Bronchoscopy and oesophagoscopy."}, {"title": "CARDIAC ANAESTHESIA", "content": "NYHA classification. Arrhythmias. Angina. Dyspnoea. Special investigations - echo cardiography, angiography. Premedication. Setting up of monitoring system. Monitoring - invasive and non-invasive. Getting ready for the case. Induction of cardiac patient, precautions to be taken. Cardiopulmonary bypass. Weaning of CPB. Transferring the patient to ICU. Care to be taken. I.C.U management. Chest tube management."}, {"title": "ANAESTHESIA OUTSIDE THE O.R.", "content": "Situations. Cath Lab. Radiology. E.C.T. Short comings."}, {"title": "DAY CARE ANAESTHESIA", "content": "Special features. Set up. Advantages. Disadvantages. Complications. Future."}, {"title": "GERIATRIC ANAESTHESIA", "content": "Physiological changes. Diseases of aging. Nervous system. Geriatric pharmacodynamics / pharmacokinetics. Postoperative nervous system dysfunction."}, {"title": "ANAESTHESIA FOR TRAUMA & SHOCK", "content": "Resuscitation. Preop investigation & assessment. Circulatory management. Management of anaesthesia. Rapid sequence induction. Other problems."}, {"title": "THORACIC ANAESTHESIA", "content": "Pulmonary function tests - bed side, Vitallograph. Preoperative preparation. Premedication. Check list. Induction, Intubation. Double lumen tubes. Monitoring. Pain management. Extubation. ICU management."}, {"title": "Postoperative problems", "content": "Nausea & Vomiting. Sore throat. Laryngeal edema, Bronchospasm. Neurological complications. Awareness. Vascular complications. Trauma to teeth. Headache. Backache. Ocular complications. Auditory complications."}, {"title": "MAJOR CATASTROPHES", "content": "Mortality. Causes of death. Cerebral damage. Prevention."}, {"title": "SYLLABUS FOR PRACTICALS", "content": "Instruments, OSPE charts."}, {"title": "Main Syllabus scope (III Year)", "content": "1. Sterilization Procedures. 2. Regional anaesthetic techniques. 3. Anaesthesia for speciality Surgeries."}], "units": [], "reference_books": [], "notes": "No reference books listed in source."}], "intro": "No reference books listed in source."}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"components": [{"name": "Theory (University)", "max": 100, "min": 50}, {"name": "Practical", "max": 100, "min": 50}, {"name": "Viva", "max": 50, "min": 25}, {"name": "Internal Assessment", "max": 50, "min": 25}], "question_pattern": {"duration_hours": null, "sections": [], "total_marks": 100}, "notes": "Exam pattern per Examination Pattern I/II/III Year tables: Theory MAX 100 / MIN 50; Practical MAX 100 / MIN 50; Viva MAX 50 / MIN 25; Internal Assessment MAX 50 (MIN shown as 20 for the first subject each year and 25 for the others). Year I: (1) BASIC SCIENCES; (2) BASICS OF COMPUTER SCIENCE AND ENGLISH. Marks in Basic Sciences to be allotted as Anatomy 30% - Physiology 30% - Biochemistry 20% & Pathology 20%. Basics of Computer Science and English will be an internal paper - Institution will send the marks to the University. Source does not specify examination duration or theory question-paper section breakdown."}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"total_duration": "One year", "postings": [], "notes": "Section header: \"POSTINGS DURING ONE YEAR INTERNSHIP\". The posting rotation lines in the source are corrupted/interleaved by OCR and cannot be reconstructed verbatim with confidence. Raw source fragments: \"Post Operative room / Recovery room - 3 months\", \"Sterilisation room ... 3 months\", \"Medical / Surgical Posting room (Including Post record room)\", \"Operation Theatre 3 months including Surgical ICU\", \"Casualty & OT\", \"General surgery OT\", \"Obstetrics & Gynaecology OT\", \"Paediatrics\", durations \"15 days / 1 month\". Postings left empty to avoid fabrication."}$ahs$::jsonb),
  ('1508', 'applied anatomy, physiology and biochemistry related to cardiac technology', 1, $ahs${"academic_year": 1, "subjects": [{"subject_no": "Paper I", "title": "applied anatomy, physiology and biochemistry related to cardiac technology", "mode": "flat", "topics": ["THEORY - BASIC ANATOMY: Introduction to Anatomy", "Basic Anatomical terminology", "Osteology - Upper limb – clavicle, scapula, humerous, radius, ulna; Lower limb - femur, hipbone, sacrum, tibia, fibula; Vertebral column", "Thorax – Intercostal space, pleura, bony thoracic cage, ribs sternum & thoracic vertebrae", "Lungs – Trachae, bronchial tree and circulation.", "Heart – Surface and gross anatomy of heart, chambers of the heart, valves of the heart, major blood Vessels of heart, pericardium, coronary arteries, pulmonary circulation and venous system.", "Myology – Muscles of thorax, muscles of upper limb (arm & fore arm); Flexor and extensor group of muscles (origin, insertion, nerve supply, action)", "Histology – Types of tissue: (a) Epithelia - Squamous, Glandular, Transitional, Cartilage; (b) Connective tissue – bone, fibrous tissue, muscle", "Excretory system – Kidney, ureters, bladder, structure of nephrons.", "PRACTICALS: Heart cut section, Anatomy of Heart and Identification of structures; Histology – Slides for identification, general features, heart muscle valve and atherosclerosis", "PHYSIOLOGY 1. Overview of the cardiovascular system - Functions of the cardiovascular system; Circulation of blood; Central control of the cardiovascular system", "PHYSIOLOGY 2. Cardiac cycle - Mechanical events; Arterial cycle and central venous pressure cycle; Clinical aspects of human cardiac cycle", "PHYSIOLOGY 3. Cardiac excitation and contraction - Mechanism of contraction; Sinoatrial node function; The cardiac conduction system; Atrioventricular node function; Autonomic regulation of the heart rate", "PHYSIOLOGY 4. Assessment of cardiac output - Fick principle; Thermodilution and indicator dilution methods; Pulse Doppler methods; Miscellaneous methods", "PHYSIOLOGY 5. Hemodynamics - Relationship between pressure, flow and resistance; Frank-Starling law; Preload, afterload and contractility; Control of stroke volume and cardiac output", "PHYSIOLOGY 6. Solute transport between blood and tissues - Circulation of fluid between plasma, interstitium lymph", "PHYSIOLOGY 7. Vascular smooth muscle - Mechanism of contraction; Pharmacomechanical coupling, automaticity", "PHYSIOLOGY 8. Control of blood vessels - Local control mechanisms; Nervous control; Hormonal control", "PHYSIOLOGY 9. Specialization in individual circulation - Coronary circulation; Cerebral circulation; Pulmonary circulation; Cutaneouos circulation", "PHYSIOLOGY 10. Cardiovascular receptors, reflexes and central control", "PHYSIOLOGY 11. Coordicated cardiovascular responses - Posture; Valsalva manoeuvre; Exercise; Divingreflex", "PHYSIOLOGY 12. Cardiovascular responses ion pathological situations - Shock and haemorrhage; Syncope; Essential hypertension; Chronic cardiac failure", "PHYSIOLOGY 13. Respiratory physiology - Mechanics of respiration; Principles of gas exchange regulation of respire", "PHYSIOLOGY 14. Hematology and coagulation physiology - blood components; Blood groups and blood transfusion; Hemostasis", "BIO-CHEMISTRY - Biomolecules and the cell: Major complex biomolecules of cell and cell organelles - Prokaryotic and eukaryotic cell", "Carbohydrates: Chemical structure, function - Classification - Monosaccharides - Disaccharides - Polysaccharides - Homopolysaccahrides - Heteropolysaccharudes - Glycoproteins", "Proteins: Amino acids - Classification - Structure of proteins - Determination of protein structure - Properties of proteins - Denaturation - Classification of proteins - Antigen, Antibody - Types, Plasma proteins - Blood clotting.", "Lipids: Chemical structure, functions, Classification - fatty acids Triacylglycerols, Phospholipids, glycoproteins, Lipoproteins - Steroids - Amphipathic 