enal disease; Digitalis and acute ionotropes – digoxin, odoubutamine, dopamine, adrenaline, noradrenaline, isoprenaline; Beta Blockers – Carvidilol, Bisoprolol, metaprolol", "PHARMACOLOGY 3. Anti-hypertensive drugs: Diuretics, beta-blockers, ACE inhibitors, calcium antagonists, direct vasodilators, centrally acting and peripherally acting vasodilators; Angiotensin Receptor Blocker – Valsartan Losartan Telmisartan olmesartan", "PHARMACOLOGY 4. Anti-arrhythmic agents: Amiodarone, adenosine, verapamil, diltiazem, lidocaine, mexiletine, Phenytoin, flecainide, bretylium, atropine, Isoprenaline", "PHARMACOLOGY 5. Antithrombotic agents: Platelet inhibitors - aspirin, clopidogrel, Prasugrel, ticagrelor; Anticoagulants - heparin, low molecular weight heparin, warfarin, fondaparinux; Fibrinolytics - streptokinase, urokinase, Tenectaplase, reteplase; Glycoprotein 2b3a antagonists - abciximab, tirofiban, eptifibatide", "PHARMACOLOGY 6. Lipid lowering and anti-atherosclerotic drugs: statins, estimibe, niacin, fenofibrate", "PHARMACOLOGY 7. Miscellaneous drugs: Protamine; Narcotics - morphine, pethidine, fentanyl; Sedatives - diazepam, midazolam; Steroids - hydrocortisone, oprednisolone; Antihistamines - diphenhydramine; Antibiotics - pecicillins, cephalosporins, aminoglycosides; Antacids and proton pump inhibitors; Anaesthetic agents - local general"], "units": [], "reference_books": [], "mark_distribution": [{"subject": "Pathology Practical", "component": "Spotters [Duration 90 minutes, Maximum 15 marks]", "marks": 3}, {"subject": "Pathology Practical", "component": "Carry out any two Investigations (Hb / PCV / WBC count / differential count / Abs Eosinophil count / P.S. staining & reporting / ESR / Retic count)", "marks": 4}, {"subject": "Pathology Practical", "component": "Urine Examination - General Physical Examination; Tests for Sugar, Ketone bodies, Blood & Proteins", "marks": 8}, {"subject": "Pathology Practical", "component": "Internal Assessment", "marks": 5}, {"subjec