ers of kidney and liver (diagnostic tests), coagulation disorders, disorders of calcium and phosphorus metabolism, endocrine disorders.", "Biochemical tests, their interpretation, radioactive isotopes in diagnosis, urine analysis"]}], "reference_books": [], "notes": "Maps First Year SUBJECT 1 ANATOMY, SUBJECT 2 PHYSIOLOGY and SUBJECT 3 BIOCHEMISTRY (each 4 units). The First Year also includes SUBJECT 4 Introduction to Computers and SUBJECT 5 Technical Report Writing/Spoken English/Patient Oriented Communication Skills, but English and Computer are internal papers with no university examination, so they are not represented as university papers in the PA paper list."}], "intro": "Maps First Year SUBJECT 1 ANATOMY, SUBJECT 2 PHYSIOLOGY and SUBJECT 3 BIOCHEMISTRY (each 4 units). The First Year also includes SUBJECT 4 Introduction to Computers and SUBJECT 5 Technical Report Writing/Spoken English/Patient Oriented Communication Skills, but English and Computer are internal papers with no university examination, so they are not represented as university papers in the PA paper list."}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"components": [{"name": "Internal Assessment", "max": 50, "min": 25}, {"name": "Theory (University)", "max": 100, "min": 50}, {"name": "Practical", "max": 50, "min": 25}], "question_pattern": {"duration_hours": null, "sections": [{"name": "Essay", "questions": 3, "marks_each": 10, "total": 30}, {"name": "Short Notes", "questions": 8, "marks_each": 5, "total": 40}, {"name": "Short Answers", "questions": 10, "marks_each": 3, "total": 30}], "total_marks": 100}, "notes": "ALLIED HEALTH SCIENCES EXAMINATION QUESTION PAPER PATTERN - B.Sc. DEGREE COURSE PHYSICIAN ASSISTANT: ESSAY 3 X 10 = 30 MARKS; SHORT NOTES 8 X 5 = 40 MARKS; SHORT ANSWERS 10 X 3 = 30 MARKS; TOTAL = 100 MARKS. Per subject: Internal Assessment (IA) Max 50 / Min 25, Theory Max 100 / Min 50, Practical Max 50 / Min 25 (no Viva for these papers). Internal Assessment breakup = Theory (20) + Practical (20) + Log Book/Project/Record (10); wherever there is no Log Book/Project/Record work the 10 marks are added to the Practical of the respective subject. I YEAR basic sciences = Anatomy, Physiology, Biochemistry, Computer, Technical Report Writing, English and Communication. English and Computer are INTERNAL papers - marks sent to the university, there is NO university examination for English and Computer papers (hence not listed as university papers here)."}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"total_duration": "12 months", "postings": [{"area": "General Medicine", "duration": "3 months"}, {"area": "Surgery", "duration": "3 months"}, {"area": "O&G", "duration": "1 month"}, {"area": "ENT", "duration": "1 month"}, {"area": "Orthopeadics", "duration": "1 month"}, {"area": "Peadiatrics", "duration": "1 month"}, {"area": "ICU", "duration": "1 month"}, {"area": "Emergency", "duration": "1 month"}], "notes": "Internship Postings - B.Sc. Physician Assistant course; Period of Internship: 12 months. The source posting/duration table is OCR-jumbled; durations printed (3 months, 3 months, 1 month, 1 month, 1 month, 1 month) map across the postings General Medicine, Surgery, O&G, ENT, Orthopeadics, Peadiatrics, ICU, Emergency to sum to 12 months (General Medicine 3 + Surgery 3 + O&G 1 + ENT 1 + Orthopeadics 1 + Peadiatrics 1 + ICU 1 + Emergency 1). Separate from this internship, the programme also has per-year IN-SERVICE TRAINING (rotation) skill checklists as PRACTICAL EXAMINATION DETAILS: FIRST YEAR - INSERVICE TRAINING I (LAB ROTATION): Training in laboratory techniques - Phlebotomy, collection of blood sample and storage; Urine collection/analysis/normal and abnormal values significance; Biochemical parameters and their normal and abnormal values/significance; Cardiac enzymes significance/troponin; Viral markers and their significance; Culture methods/techniques/swab etc.; CSF/Pleural fluid/Ascitic fluid analysis and their significance; Mantoux test and its significance; Viral markers/HIV testing interpretation; Pregnancy test; Sterile techniques/sterilization of lab; Instruments and their importance; Microscope; Blood counts and ESR; Slide preparation/staining; Malarial parasite identification and its test; Motion analysis; Disposing lab waste materials; Entering the data into the computer system; Giving a scenario - ask to interpret to the doctor and to the patient. Basic science: Bones and their identification; Slides - Columnar, ciliated columnar, squamous, cuboidal epithelia; Pictures identification. SECOND YEAR - INSERVICE TRAINING II (CLINICAL DEPARTMENT ROTATION): Case sheet writing; Assessment of communication to the patient; BLS (demonstration of basic life support); Ryle's tube, Foley's, colostomy, drains care; Anaesthesiology - assisting the anaesthetist and different techniques of anaesthesia; Giving a common drug strip and asking questions; Giving an ECG strip and asking basic questions; ECG taking and interpretation - common cases only; LP/Pleural tapping/ascetic fluid tapping and other common procedures - providing a scenario and asking questions; Normal chest X-ray presentation/common abnormal pattern; Normal delivery; Neonatal care and resuscitation; Obs and Gyn instruments/sterile techniques/instruments (forceps etc); Importance of PAP Smear/terminal care; Preparing the discharge summaries; Entry of biochemical values into the patient's file; Assess the communication skills by giving a scenario. THIRD YEAR - INSERVICE TRAINING III (SURGICAL DEPARTMENT ROTATION): Case sheet writing; Vitals - normal and abnormal values and their significance; ECG interpretation/USG significance; Life style modifications and their importance - giving some examples and asking questions; Surgical instruments and their sterilization procedures; Dressing materials and different techniques; Wound care/trauma patient care; Dealing with an unconscious patient; Assisting surgeons; Shifting of trauma patient; Care of the terminally ill patient; Bed sore and its care; Burns patient and their care; ICU protocols; Blood transfusions; Discharge summary preparation; Angio report typing; Entering the biochemical values and their interpretation; Giving a scenario in surgery and assessing the communication skills."}$ahs$::jsonb),
