s LSCS, third trimester bleeding, preeclampsia and eclampsia, medical disorders complicating pregnancy, surgical emergencies in obstetrics, Rh iso immunization, partogram, ultra sound in obstetrics, fetal monitoring, active management of labour, neonatal resuscitation, analgesia and anaesthesia in obstetrics, instrumental deliveries, LSCS, third stage complications, normal and abnormal puerperium, morbidity and mortality, medical auditing in obstetrics."]}, {"unit_no": "Obstetrics & Gynaecology - Unit 3", "topics": ["Gynecology: - Maldevelopment, injuries, infections, cysts, tumors of female genital tract.", "Vulva - inflammation, ulcers, atrophy, dystrophies, cysts, neoplasm", "Vagina - leucorrhoea, infections, carcinoma", "Cervix - erosion, ulcer, dysplasia, carcinoma", "Uterus - prolapse, displacements (inversion and retroversion), endometriosis abnormal uterine bleeding / post menopausal bleeding, endometrial hyperplasia, benign and malignant tumours.", "Primary and secondary amenorrhoea, infertility, PCOD, assisted reproductive techniques, choriocarcinoma,"]}, {"unit_no": "Obstetrics & Gynaecology - Unit 4", "topics": ["Urinary system - Stress incontinence, pelvic pain, low back ache", "Cancer screening for genital malignancy and breast / Pap smear", "Radiotherapy outline and chemotherapy", "Neonatology: - Neonatal resuscitation, meconium aspiration syndrome, preterm care, RDS, neonatal jaundice, congenital anomalies, birth injuries."]}], "reference_books": [], "notes": "Maps Second Year SUBJECT 7 SURGERY/EQUIPMENTS/ANAESTHESIOLOGY (4 units) plus SUBJECT 10 OBSTETRICS AND GYNAECOLOGY (4 units)."}], "intro": "Maps Second Year SUBJECT 7 SURGERY/EQUIPMENTS/ANAESTHESIOLOGY (4 units) plus SUBJECT 10 OBSTETRICS AND GYNAECOLOGY (4 units)."}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"components": [{"name": "Internal Assessment", "max": 50, "min": 25}, {"name": "Theory (University)", "max": 100, "min": 50}, {"name": "Practical", "max": 50, "min": 25}], "question_pattern": {"duration_hours": null, "sections": [{"name": "Essay", "questions": 3, "marks_each": 10, "total": 30}, {"name": "Short Notes", "questions": 8, "marks_each": 5, "total": 40}, {"name": "Short Answers", "questions": 10, "marks_each": 3, "total": 30}], "total_marks": 100}, "notes": "ALLIED HEALTH SCIENCES EXAMINATION QUESTION PAPER PATTERN - B.Sc. DEGREE COURSE PHYSICIAN ASSISTANT: ESSAY 3 X 10 = 30 MARKS; SHORT NOTES 8 X 5 = 40 MARKS; SHORT ANSWERS 10 X 3 = 30 MARKS; TOTAL = 100 MARKS. Per subject: Internal Assessment (IA) Max 50 / Min 25, Theory Max 100 / Min 50, Practical Max 50 / Min 25 (no Viva for these papers). Internal Assessment breakup = Theory (20) + Practical (20) + Log Book/Project/Record (10); wherever there is no Log Book/Project/Record work the 10 marks are added to the Practical of the respective subject. I YEAR basic sciences = Anatomy, Physiology, Biochemistry, Computer, Technical Report Writing, English and Communication. English and Computer are INTERNAL papers - marks sent to the university, there is NO university examination for English and Computer papers (hence not listed as university papers here)."}$ahs$::jsonb, $ahs${"total_duration": "12 months", "postings": [{"area": "General Medicine", "duration": "3 months"}, {"area": "Surgery", "duration": "3 months"}, {"area": "O&G", "duration": "1 month"}, {"area": "ENT", "duration": "1 month"}, {"area": "Orthopeadics", "duration": "1 month"}, {"area": "Peadiatrics", "duration": "1 month"}, {"area": "ICU", "duration": "1 month"}, {"area": "Emergency", "duration": "1 month"}], "notes": "Internship Postings - B.Sc. Physician Assistant course; Period of Internship: 12 months. The source posting/duration table is OCR-jumbled; durations printed (3 months, 3 months, 1 month, 1 month, 1 month, 1 month) map across the postings General Medicine, Surgery, O&G, ENT, Orthopeadics, Peadiatrics, ICU, Emergency to sum to 12 months (General Medicine 3 + Surgery 3 + O&G 1 + ENT 1 + Orthopeadics 1 + Peadiatrics 1 + ICU 1 + Emergency 1). Separate from this internship, the programme also has per-year IN-SERVICE TRAINING (rotation) skill checklists as PRACTICAL EXAMINATION DETAILS: FIRST YEAR - INSERVICE TRAINING I (LAB ROTATION): Training in laboratory techniques - Phlebotomy, collection of blood sample and storage; Urine collection/analysis/normal and abnormal values significance; Biochemical parameters and their normal and abnormal values/significance; Cardiac enzymes significance/troponin; Viral markers and their significance; Culture methods/techniques/swab etc.; CSF/Pleural fluid/Ascitic fluid analysis and their significance; Mantoux test and its significance; Viral markers/HIV testing interpretation; Pregnancy test; Sterile techniques/sterilization of lab; Instruments and their importance; Microscope; Blood counts and ESR; Slide preparation/staining; Malarial parasite identification and its test; Motion analysis; Disposing lab waste materials; Entering the data into the computer system; Giving a scenario - ask to interpret to the doctor and to the patient. Basic science: Bones and their identification; Slides - Columnar, ciliated columnar, squamous, cuboidal epithelia; Pictures identification. SECOND YEAR - INSERVICE TRAINING II (CLINICAL DEPARTMENT ROTATION): Case sheet writing; Assessment of communication to the patient; BLS (demonstration of basic life support); Ryle's tube, Foley's, colostomy, drains care; Anaesthesiology - assisting the anaesthetist and different techniques of anaesthesia; Giving a common drug strip and asking questions; Giving an ECG strip and asking basic questions; ECG taking and interpretation - common cases only; LP/Pleural tapping/ascetic fluid tapping and other common procedures - providing a scenario and asking questions; Normal chest X-ray presentation/common abnormal pattern; Normal delivery; Neonatal care and resuscitation; Obs and Gyn instruments/sterile techniques/instruments (forceps etc); Importance of PAP Smear/terminal care; Preparing the discharge summaries; Entry of biochemical values into the patient's file; Assess the communication skills by giving a scenario. THIRD YEAR - INSERVICE TRAINING III (SURGICAL DEPARTMENT ROTATION): Case sheet writing; Vitals - normal and abnormal values and their significance; ECG interpretation/USG significance; Life style modifications and their importance - giving some examples and asking questions; Surgical instruments and their sterilization procedures; Dressing materials and different techniques; Wound care/trauma patient care; Dealing with an unconscious patient; Assisting surgeons; Shifting of trauma patient; Care of the terminally ill patient; Bed sore and its care; Burns patient and their care; ICU protocols; Blood transfusions; Discharge summary preparation; Angio report typing; Entering the biochemical values and their interpretation; Giving a scenario in surgery and assessing the communication skills."}$ahs$::jsonb),
  ('1621', 'Cardiology and cardiac surgery/Neurology.', 3, $ahs${"academic_year": 3, "subjects": [{"subject_no": "Paper I", "title": "Cardiology and cardiac surgery/Neurology.", "mode": "units", "topics": [], "units": [{"unit_no": "Cardiology & Cardiac Surgery - Unit 1", "topics": ["Basics - structural basis of cardiovascular disease, embryology, chambers, heart valves, surface marking, great vessels, blood, cardiovascular disease, cardiac cycle, heart sounds, circulation of blood, cardiovascular responses to exercise, heart failure and compensatory mechanism, cardiac muscle action, coronary perfusion."]}, {"unit_no": "Cardiology & Cardiac Surgery - Unit 2", "topics": ["Cardiovascular diseases - symptoms and signs, pulse, BP, JVP", "Congenital heart disease - cyanotic and acyanotic heart diseases", "Hypertension- essential, malignant, systemic and pulmonary hypertensions", "Arterial diseases - atherosclerosis - risk factors, Burger's disease", "Coronary, Rheumatic heart disease, heart failure, cardiac arrhythmias, cardiomyopathies", "Peripheral vascular disease, pulmonary thromboembolism,", "Systemic diseases affecting the heart, pregnancy and heart disease", "Pericardial diseases, Cardiac trauma, tumors of heart"]}, {"unit_no": "Cardiology & Cardiac Surgery - Unit 3", "topics": ["Prevention of heart diseases - Diagnostic tools - ECG, Chest X-ray, ECHO, TMT, Holter, 24 hour ambulatory BP monitoring, blood analysis., etc.", "Cardiac catheterization and coronary angiography- preparation of patient physically and mentally. Pre and post-operative care and rehabilitation programme. PPI", "Importance of life style modification measures."]}, {"unit_no": "Cardiology & Cardiac Surgery - Unit 4", "topics": ["Cardiac surgery ;- Basics - Cardiopulmonary bypass - closed and open heart operation, PDA ligation, closed mitral valvotomy, pulmonary artery banding, block trussing shunt, pericardiectomy, shunt operations, ASD and VSD closure, Tetralogy of Fallot correction, valvular di